{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "01215",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 1.07,
      "end_seconds": 6.33,
      "duration_seconds": 5.26,
      "text": "Hi, doctor, I came as soon as they called me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 7.67,
      "end_seconds": 12.14,
      "duration_seconds": 4.47,
      "text": "No problem at all, come in. What's troubling you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 12.76,
      "end_seconds": 15.65,
      "duration_seconds": 2.89,
      "text": "Doctor, thank you for seeing us."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 16.87,
      "end_seconds": 20.74,
      "duration_seconds": 3.87,
      "text": "That's fine, sit down. We'll go through it together."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 21.35,
      "end_seconds": 29.51,
      "duration_seconds": 8.16,
      "text": "It's, It's a dry cough in the evenings, doctor. He didn't want to come, but I insisted."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 35.51,
      "end_seconds": 38.72,
      "duration_seconds": 3.21,
      "text": "How many days or weeks has it been?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 39.44,
      "end_seconds": 43.33,
      "duration_seconds": 3.89,
      "text": "Right, um, I'd say three weeks, maybe."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 44.37,
      "end_seconds": 48.04,
      "duration_seconds": 3.67,
      "text": "It was closer to a month, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 50.04,
      "end_seconds": 54.19,
      "duration_seconds": 4.15,
      "text": "Okay, so roughly three to four weeks. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 55.15,
      "end_seconds": 56.38,
      "duration_seconds": 1.23,
      "text": "Yeah, roughly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 57.04,
      "end_seconds": 66.49,
      "duration_seconds": 9.45,
      "text": "Can you describe it a bit more for me? How strong it is, what the pattern is, what helps."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 67.47,
      "end_seconds": 71.43,
      "duration_seconds": 3.96,
      "text": "It settles a little with antihistamine. Mostly moderate."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 72.05,
      "end_seconds": 74.81,
      "duration_seconds": 2.76,
      "text": "Does anything else come with it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 75.62,
      "end_seconds": 81.26,
      "duration_seconds": 5.64,
      "text": "When it starts I tend to get itchy eyes as well."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 81.81,
      "end_seconds": 91.63,
      "duration_seconds": 9.82,
      "text": "Sorry, what was I saying, and the other thing I wanted to mention is that I can't really—"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 91.73,
      "end_seconds": 97.72,
      "duration_seconds": 5.99,
      "text": "Tell the doctor about the other thing, uh, that's what worries me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 98.4,
      "end_seconds": 100.97,
      "duration_seconds": 2.57,
      "text": "I was getting to that!"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 104.77,
      "end_seconds": 107.33,
      "duration_seconds": 2.56,
      "text": "Is it constant or in episodes?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 108.08,
      "end_seconds": 111.32,
      "duration_seconds": 3.24,
      "text": "I'd say a few times a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 112.19,
      "end_seconds": 114.93,
      "duration_seconds": 2.74,
      "text": "Is it bearing on you a lot?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 116.27,
      "end_seconds": 122.14,
      "duration_seconds": 5.87,
      "text": "Well, it's... hard to say, it's kind of... I don't know—"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 123.64,
      "end_seconds": 129.32,
      "duration_seconds": 5.68,
      "text": "Take your time. Mild, moderate, or severe, if you had to pick?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 130.96,
      "end_seconds": 135.47,
      "duration_seconds": 4.51,
      "text": "I, I'd give it a eight, out of ten."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 137.36,
      "end_seconds": 144.66,
      "duration_seconds": 7.3,
      "text": "Have you had a dry cough in the evenings before, or is this the first time?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 146.07,
      "end_seconds": 153.47,
      "duration_seconds": 7.4,
      "text": "A bit, a couple of years ago. It settled by itself back then."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_5",
      "role": "UNKNOWN",
      "start_seconds": 154.32,
      "end_seconds": 157.4,
      "duration_seconds": 3.08,
      "text": "Mm, that's what happened, yes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 158.6,
      "end_seconds": 161.91,
      "duration_seconds": 3.31,
      "text": "I'll just record a few vital signs."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 175.38,
      "end_seconds": 177.43,
      "duration_seconds": 2.05,
      "text": "Nearly done with the readings..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 190.11,
      "end_seconds": 199.5,
      "duration_seconds": 9.39,
      "text": "Okay: pressure 126 over 69, respiratory rate 15, pulse 76, oxygen saturation is 99 percent, temperature is 36.9 degrees."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 200.54,
      "end_seconds": 202.13,
      "duration_seconds": 1.59,
      "text": "Is that okay?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 203.0,
      "end_seconds": 206.26,
      "duration_seconds": 3.26,
      "text": "Don't worry, we'll discuss it in a second."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 209.23,
      "end_seconds": 212.9,
      "duration_seconds": 3.67,
      "text": "Let me look at the area, I'll be gentle."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 213.9,
      "end_seconds": 216.39,
      "duration_seconds": 2.49,
      "text": "Yeah, uh, no problem."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 217.31,
      "end_seconds": 218.69,
      "duration_seconds": 1.38,
      "text": "Nearly finished here."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 230.02,
      "end_seconds": 234.98,
      "duration_seconds": 4.96,
      "text": "Your chest is clear and your nose looks a little swollen inside."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 236.94,
      "end_seconds": 239.45,
      "duration_seconds": 2.51,
      "text": "Yeah, um, no problem."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 243.98,
      "end_seconds": 249.16,
      "duration_seconds": 5.18,
      "text": "You can relax now. And what about wheeze, shortness of breath or fever?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 254.82,
      "end_seconds": 267.71,
      "duration_seconds": 12.89,
      "text": "No, no wheeze, no shortness of breath, no fever. I did have sneezing fits at one point, but that went away on its own."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 268.87,
      "end_seconds": 270.9,
      "duration_seconds": 2.03,
      "text": "Any trouble with the waterworks?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 271.94,
      "end_seconds": 273.59,
      "duration_seconds": 1.65,
      "text": "No changes there."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 278.26,
      "end_seconds": 281.71,
      "duration_seconds": 3.45,
      "text": "Okay, how are your bowels, any trouble?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 283.23,
      "end_seconds": 285.79,
      "duration_seconds": 2.56,
      "text": "Bowels are regular, nothing odd."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 286.72,
      "end_seconds": 290.25,
      "duration_seconds": 3.53,
      "text": "Anything in your past medical history I should know?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 291.37,
      "end_seconds": 306.71,
      "duration_seconds": 15.34,
      "text": "An underactive thyroid, for two years. Yes, gout. I'd rather know what's going on than keep guessing. I've had an irregular heartbeat, yes. I've had heart failure for about a year now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 312.09,
      "end_seconds": 320.84,
      "duration_seconds": 8.75,
      "text": "Understood. Yes, an underactive thyroid and gout are known to us, good to have that clear. How about smoking?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 321.84,
      "end_seconds": 325.49,
      "duration_seconds": 3.65,
      "text": "No, I've never smoked in my life."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 326.01,
      "end_seconds": 327.66,
      "duration_seconds": 1.65,
      "text": "Who lives with you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 329.31,
      "end_seconds": 331.81,
      "duration_seconds": 2.5,
      "text": "My partner and our baby."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 333.46,
      "end_seconds": 334.79,
      "duration_seconds": 1.33,
      "text": "What's your work?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 335.8,
      "end_seconds": 340.3,
      "duration_seconds": 4.5,
      "text": "I'm a plumber, lots of bending and kneeling."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 342.14,
      "end_seconds": 344.64,
      "duration_seconds": 2.5,
      "text": "Tell me your medicines, please."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 345.18,
      "end_seconds": 350.56,
      "duration_seconds": 5.38,
      "text": "something called eltr... Eltroxin, 100 micrograms, maybe, every morning."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 352.5,
      "end_seconds": 356.46,
      "duration_seconds": 3.96,
      "text": "Do you have the packet or the prescription with you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 357.2,
      "end_seconds": 374.83,
      "duration_seconds": 17.63,
      "text": "Not with me. I'll bring it next time. I'm, I'm on febuxostat, 80 milligrams, once a day. I'm on bisoprolol, 2.5 milligrams, once a day. Metoprolol, 50 milligrams, twice a day for my heart."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0055",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 376.42,
      "end_seconds": 379.71,
      "duration_seconds": 3.29,
      "text": "Has anyone in your family had anything serious?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0056",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 381.26,
      "end_seconds": 384.55,
      "duration_seconds": 3.29,
      "text": "My mother has an underactive thyroid."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0057",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 398.4,
      "end_seconds": 402.8,
      "duration_seconds": 4.4,
      "text": "Has anything ever caused you a reaction? I mean any allergies."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0058",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 403.63,
      "end_seconds": 405.02,
      "duration_seconds": 1.39,
      "text": "No known allergies."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0059",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 405.85,
      "end_seconds": 414.01,
      "duration_seconds": 8.16,
      "text": "Actually, I remember he had some kind of reaction to naproxen before. I couldn't swear to it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0060",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 414.98,
      "end_seconds": 417.29,
      "duration_seconds": 2.31,
      "text": "Really? I don't think so."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0061",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 417.96,
      "end_seconds": 423.19,
      "duration_seconds": 5.23,
      "text": "Alright, so that's unclear. I'll record what each of you said."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0062",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 433.51,
      "end_seconds": 444.25,
      "duration_seconds": 10.74,
      "text": "So where does that leave us? I can't pin this down yet. We're looking at seasonal hay fever causing the cough or early asthma."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0063",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 445.31,
      "end_seconds": 449.09,
      "duration_seconds": 3.78,
      "text": "Uh, what are the odds it's serious?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0064",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 449.86,
      "end_seconds": 468.28,
      "duration_seconds": 18.42,
      "text": "Nothing I've seen today points to an emergency. It looks like seasonal hay fever causing the cough. I'd like you to take fluticasone nasal spray, 50 micrograms, once a day, for the season. That's for hay fever."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0065",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 469.45,
      "end_seconds": 473.9,
      "duration_seconds": 4.45,
      "text": "So, can I collect it from my own pharmacy?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0066",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 475.16,
      "end_seconds": 485.08,
      "duration_seconds": 9.92,
      "text": "And please bring the latest prescription or the medicine boxes to the next visit, so we can settle the dose."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0067",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 486.24,
      "end_seconds": 487.74,
      "duration_seconds": 1.5,
      "text": "Okay, makes sense."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0068",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 489.65,
      "end_seconds": 493.68,
      "duration_seconds": 4.03,
      "text": "That's everything on my side. Anything you're unsure about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0069",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 495.73,
      "end_seconds": 497.87,
      "duration_seconds": 2.14,
      "text": "Thank you, doctor, goodbye."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0070",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 499.28,
      "end_seconds": 500.74,
      "duration_seconds": 1.46,
      "text": "Goodbye for now."
    }
  ]
}